SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a stripe's end piece whose contact on one face stands still is
one face with the piece before it (mitcad#236).

An analytic blend along two edges of one line (an edge split by a vertex
where nothing else meets it) whose contact on one face ends at the first
edge's end (0282's floor contact at the hole's side) gives the second
edge a piece with that contact standing still and the other running on,
for the corner to cut. The corner then cut that piece off along a section
at the first piece's end ("shrink"): the blend was two faces where the
bodies stored in the .f3d files have one.

- ChFi3d_JoinStandingEnd (after the stripe's pieces are computed): such
  an end piece that meets the piece before it in a whole section, between
  the same faces with the same orientation, on the same analytic surface
  (parametrized the same, or otherwise by a plane isometry with the same
  normals, ChFi3d_AnalyticParamMap of 0241) takes that piece's surface,
  its p-curves on the blend mapped onto it.
- PerformIntersectionAtEnd: where the piece before the end piece is on
  the end piece's own surface, no section is put between them.

Upstream: new.
